# samples/10-CachingAndRateLimits – start it with: dotnet run --project samples/10-CachingAndRateLimits
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5110

### Cache-Control, ETag – and the output cache: send it twice, "call" stays the same
# @name price
GET {{baseUrl}}/prices/ANV-1

### 304 Not Modified – the ETag of the response above (paste it if your client doesn't support response headers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/prices/ANV-1
If-None-Match: {{price.response.headers.ETag}}

### One output cache entry per language
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog
Accept-Language: pl

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog
Accept-Language: en

### no-store – a new "call" every time
GET {{baseUrl}}/balance

### 3 per minute – send it four times: 200, 200, 200, 429 with Retry-After
GET {{baseUrl}}/quotes

### Per API key – 5 per minute, 20 per day
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=anvil
X-Api-Key: key-a

### …another key, another budget
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=anvil
X-Api-Key: key-b

### Token bucket: bursts of 2, one more every 10 s
POST {{baseUrl}}/exports

### The definitions with their caching and rateLimit settings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/endpoints
